          "title": "Three Learning Paradigms",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. The Paradigms",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{blue:Supervised}: learn X → y from ==labelled== examples",
                "Regression = continuous value; classification = category",
                "{green:Unsupervised}: structure in ==unlabelled== X only",
                "Clustering (k-means), PCA, anomaly detection",
                "{purple:RL}: agent learns a ==policy== maximising cumulative reward",
                "No labelled answers; feedback is ==delayed=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Agent",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Action",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Environment",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Reward",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Compared",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Paradigm",
                "Feedback",
                "Example"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Supervised",
                  "label per example",
                  "spam filter"
                ],
                [
                  "Unsupervised",
                  "no labels",
                  "customer segments"
                ],
                [
                  "RL",
                  "reward signal",
                  "game-playing agent"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Quick test",
              "text": "Label, no label, or a ==reward==?"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**House price?** Regression: the target is continuous",
                "**RL vs supervised?** RL gets delayed rewards, not a label per example",
                "**Clustering accuracy?** No: there are no true labels to compare against"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Features, Labels and Data Splits",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Features, Labels and Data Splits",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Data and the three sets",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{blue:Features} = input columns ==X==",
                "{green:Label} (target) = column ==y== the model predicts",
                "One **row** = one example"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Set",
                "Job"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Train",
                  "fits model **parameters**"
                ],
                [
                  "Validation",
                  "tunes **hyperparameters**, picks the model"
                ],
                [
                  "Test",
                  "one final **unbiased** estimate"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Split choices",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Typical split: ==60/20/20== or ==70/15/15==",
                "**Imbalanced classes**: stratified split",
                "**Time series**: time-ordered split, never random"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Data leakage",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Scaler, imputer or feature selection fitted on **full data** leaks test information",
                "Fit on ==train only==, then transform val/test: use a Pipeline"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "from sklearn.pipeline import make_pipeline",
                "pipe = make_pipeline(StandardScaler(), SVC())",
                "pipe.fit(X_train, y_train)  # scaler sees train only",
                "pipe.score(X_val, y_val)  # reuses train mean/std"
              ],
              "note": "preprocessing lives inside the pipeline"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why validation and test?** Tuning on validation makes it optimistic; untouched test gives the honest score",
                "**Data leakage?** Test information reaching training; fit preprocessing on train only, inside a Pipeline",
                "**Time-series split?** Order by time: train on the past, test on the future"
              ],
              "style": "number"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Overfitting and Underfitting",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Overfitting and Underfitting",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Spot the Fit",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Case",
                "Train error",
                "Val error"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "{blue:Underfit}: model too simple",
                  "high",
                  "high"
                ],
                [
                  "{red:Overfit}: memorises noise",
                  "low",
                  "==much higher=="
                ],
                [
                  "Good fit",
                  "low",
                  "low, close to train"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Diagnose with Learning Curves",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Too simple",
                    "sub": "both errors high",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Sweet spot",
                    "sub": "val error minimum",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Too complex",
                    "sub": "train falls, val rises",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Plot error vs ==training size==, or error vs ==model complexity==",
                "Val error ==bottoms out, then rises== as complexity grows",
                "The ==train-val gap== is the overfit symptom"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Fixes",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Overfit (big gap)",
                "Underfit (both high)"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "More data",
                  "More capacity"
                ],
                [
                  "Regularise: L1/L2, dropout",
                  "Better features"
                ],
                [
                  "Simpler model",
                  "Less regularisation"
                ],
                [
                  "Early stopping",
                  "Train longer"
                ],
                [
                  "Fewer features",
                  "—"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Data fixes variance only",
              "text": "More rows cannot rescue a model too simple to fit them. Add capacity or features."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**99% train, 70% test?** Overfit (large gap): add data, regularise, simplify, early stop",
                "**Early stopping?** Halts training once val error starts rising, before noise is memorised",
                "**More data fixes underfitting?** No: the model lacks capacity, so add capacity or features"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Bias-Variance Trade-off",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Bias-Variance Trade-off",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Error Decomposition",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Expected error = ==bias²== + ==variance== + **irreducible noise**",
                "Noise is in the data: {red:no model can remove it}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Bias vs Variance",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Bias",
                "Variance"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Cause",
                  "Wrong assumptions",
                  "Sensitive to the sample"
                ],
                [
                  "Symptom",
                  "Misses true pattern",
                  "Predictions swing between samples"
                ],
                [
                  "Means",
                  "{blue:Underfit}",
                  "{red:Overfit}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "More complexity",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Bias falls",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Variance rises",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Sweet spot",
                    "sub": "lowest total",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Models and Ensembles",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Model / method",
                "Effect"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Linear regression",
                  "High bias, low variance"
                ],
                [
                  "Deep decision tree",
                  "Low bias, high variance"
                ],
                [
                  "Bagging, random forest",
                  "{green:Cut variance}"
                ],
                [
                  "Boosting",
                  "{green:Cuts bias}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Mistake",
              "text": "Zero train error is not low total error: past the sweet spot, ==variance== wins."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Bias vs variance?** Line on curved data misses it (bias); deep tree changes per sample (variance)",
                "**Why a trade-off?** Complexity cuts bias but raises variance, so total error is U-shaped",
                "**Which ensemble?** Bagging cuts variance; boosting cuts bias"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
